# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two rules earn their place here beyond the usual size trimming:
#   - .env is excluded so a developer's real secrets can never be baked into a
#     layer. An image is not a secret store; anyone who can pull it can read
#     every layer. Config arrives at run time through the environment.
#   - apps/desktop is excluded so the Electron shell (and its ~200MB electron
#     devDependency) stays out of a server image that never renders a window.
#
# Note the previous version used bare `dist` and `.next`, which match only at
# the context root — the real build output lives at apps/web/.next. Patterns
# below are rooted with **/ so they match at any depth.

# ─── Dependencies (reinstalled in-image; host binaries are the wrong ABI) ────
node_modules
**/node_modules

# ─── Secrets — never, under any circumstances, in an image layer ─────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ─── Build output (regenerated inside the image) ─────────────────────────────
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Prisma client — regenerated in the build stage against the in-image schema.
apps/api/src/generated

# ─── The Electron desktop app: not a server-side service ─────────────────────
apps/desktop

# ─── Runtime + test leftovers ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.artifacts
.qaai-runs
.localdev
.generated
test-results
playwright-report
coverage
**/*.log

# ─── VCS, CI and editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
**/.DS_Store

# ─── Deployment descriptors (not needed at run time) ─────────────────────────
docs
deploy
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yml.example
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
